---
# The C half of the tree: this directory and tests/test_plugin are the only translation units the
# repository compiles as C, and two checks of the root config describe C++ rather than a defect here.
# Scoped to the directory rather than switched off globally, because both are worth keeping over the
# C++ that is the rest of the codebase.
InheritParentConfig: true

# cppcoreguidelines-init-variables wants an initialiser on every declaration, and these files declare
# at the top of the block and assign below — which is how C reads and, more to the point, what makes a
# use before the assignment a diagnosable mistake rather than a silent zero. Seeding a handle with 0
# would hide exactly the bug the check exists to find.
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-init-variables
...
